{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/2026-07-15-how-small-habits-become-easier/audio/main-fdf730fd0ec0.mp3","durationSec":114.804,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":4.04,"text":"A cue is a small signal that tells your brain, \"Time to do this now.\""},{"start":4.84,"end":7.94,"text":"It can be a time, a place, or an action you already do."},{"start":7.94,"end":15.44,"text":"Researchers Lally and colleagues at University College London studied 96 people who tried to build a new daily habit."},{"start":16.48,"end":25.7,"text":"Each person chose a clear cue, like \"after breakfast,\" and then did one small action, like eating a piece of fruit."},{"start":26.62,"end":30.34,"text":"When the cue was the same every day, the action became automatic faster."},{"start":31.32,"end":34.4,"text":"A weak or changing cue made the habit much harder to keep."},{"start":35.3,"end":39.8,"text":"Doing the same small action after the same cue, day after day, is called repetition."},{"start":40.6,"end":44.7,"text":"In the same study, the action felt more automatic each time people did it."},{"start":45.18,"end":51.02,"text":"At first, the line on their chart went up quickly: the second and third days felt much easier than the first."},{"start":52.02,"end":55.4,"text":"Later, the line got flatter, but the habit kept growing."},{"start":56.08,"end":60.82,"text":"On average, people needed about 66 days before the action felt truly automatic."},{"start":62.04,"end":67.3,"text":"Some habits, like drinking a glass of water after breakfast, became automatic in around 20 days."},{"start":68.34,"end":74.02,"text":"Harder habits, like doing 50 sit-ups after coffee, took much longer."},{"start":75.12,"end":77.96,"text":"A tiny action is easier to repeat than a big one."},{"start":78.8,"end":81.12,"text":"Imagine two people who want to read more."},{"start":81.94,"end":85.72,"text":"Maria puts one book next to her coffee cup every night."},{"start":86.52,"end":92.64,"text":"Her cue is \"after I pour my coffee in the morning,\" and her action is \"read one page.\""},{"start":94.06,"end":96.94,"text":"Tom tells himself he will read for one hour every day."},{"start":97.3,"end":102.4,"text":"On busy days, Maria still reads her one page, so her habit grows."},{"start":103.34,"end":107.54,"text":"Tom often skips his hour, so his cue and action never connect."},{"start":108.44,"end":114.34,"text":"Small actions win because they still happen when you are tired, late, or not in the mood."}],"words":[{"text":"A","start":0,"end":0.14},{"text":"cue","start":0.14,"end":0.44},{"text":"is","start":0.44,"end":0.7},{"text":"a","start":0.7,"end":0.9},{"text":"small","start":0.9,"end":1.16},{"text":"signal","start":1.16,"end":1.5},{"text":"that","start":1.5,"end":1.68},{"text":"tells","start":1.68,"end":1.84},{"text":"your","start":1.84,"end":2.04},{"text":"brain","start":2.04,"end":2.36},{"text":"Time","start":2.82,"end":3.02},{"text":"to","start":3.02,"end":3.28},{"text":"do","start":3.28,"end":3.46},{"text":"this","start":3.46,"end":3.68},{"text":"now","start":3.68,"end":4.04},{"text":"It","start":4.84,"end":4.96},{"text":"can","start":4.96,"end":5.1},{"text":"be","start":5.1,"end":5.26},{"text":"a","start":5.26,"end":5.4},{"text":"time","start":5.4,"end":5.78},{"text":"a","start":5.92,"end":6},{"text":"place","start":6,"end":6.32},{"text":"or","start":6.48,"end":6.64},{"text":"an","start":6.64,"end":6.74},{"text":"action","start":6.74,"end":7.12},{"text":"you","start":7.12,"end":7.3},{"text":"already","start":7.3,"end":7.54},{"text":"do","start":7.54,"end":7.94},{"text":"Researchers","start":7.94,"end":9.72},{"text":"Lally","start":9.72,"end":9.8},{"text":"and","start":10,"end":10.06},{"text":"colleagues","start":10.06,"end":10.44},{"text":"at","start":10.44,"end":10.66},{"text":"University","start":10.66,"end":11.06},{"text":"College","start":11.06,"end":11.54},{"text":"London","start":11.54,"end":11.92},{"text":"studied","start":11.92,"end"